'''Michael Haigney''' is an American voice actor, voice director, and English-language adaptation writer who was one of the original voice actors of [[4Kids Entertainment]] for its [[dub]] of {{aniseries|PTS}}.

==Biography==
Haigney was the original voice director on Pokémon from the [[S01|first season]] through the [[S03|third season]], and was also one of the original voice actors, originally providing fill-in voices for Pokémon that had not been cast; under this capacity, he went under the alias '''Roger Kay'''. During the [[S06|sixth season]], Haigney left the series. After his departure, stock footage was used to voice [[Ash's Snorlax]] in ''[[AG149|Wheel Of Frontier]]'', as well as [[Brock's Geodude]] in ''[[AG177|Grating Spaces!]]''.

In the DVD commentary for ''[[M04|Celebi: The Voice of the Forest]]'', Haigney explained that he didn't realize Charmander would become a major character, believing it to only be a [[character of the day]].

In 2022, Haigney started a Podcast series called ''Original Pokéman'' where he would share memories, mysteries, and behind-the-scenes stories on the episodes that he adapted and directed.

